  "worked_solution": "The period of $y=cos\u2061x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for an integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\ncos\u2061x=cos\u2061(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-5$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos\u2061x=cos\u2061(x+2\\cdot (-5)\\cdot \\pi )=cos\u2061(x-10\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $cos\u2061x=\\frac{3}{8},$ then $cos\u2061(x-10\\pi )=\\frac{3}{8}.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4cos\u2061(x-10\\pi )+5 & =4(\\frac{3}{8})+5 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}+5 \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
